---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

/*
 * ariada.org/privacy — the privacy statement the browser extension's store
 * listing points at, and the one covering this site.
 *
 * It is short because there is little to say: the extension makes no network
 * requests at all, and the site sets no cookies and runs no analytics. Written
 * to be read rather than to be defensible — a policy nobody finishes is not a
 * disclosure.
 */

const lastRevised = "2026-08-02";
const organisation = "Agonist Development AB";
const orgNr = "559452-5726";
const contact = "hello@ariada.org";
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What Ariada does and does not do with your data.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Short version: the browser extension sends nothing anywhere, and this site
      does not watch you.
    </p>

    <h2>The browser extension</h2>
    <p>
      The extension reads the page you are looking at, in your browser, to work
      out which accessibility and compliance requirements it fails. That reading
      happens in the page itself and the result is shown in the side panel.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>It makes no network requests of any kind.</strong> There is no
      analytics, no error reporting, no licence check and no update ping. Page
      content, scan results, and the addresses you visit are never transmitted,
      because there is nothing in the extension that transmits.
    </p>
    <p>
      It stores your own settings — which requirement domains you have selected,
      and any rule modules you have added — in the browser's local storage on
      your machine. A few kilobytes of preferences. Nothing is synchronised
      between devices, and removing the extension removes them.
    </p>
    <p>
      A report is written to a file only when you ask for one, and it goes where
      you save it.
    </p>

    <h2>Permissions, and why each exists</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>Access to the current tab</dt>
      <dd>
        Granted when you open the panel and press Scan, for that one page. The
        extension has no standing access to your browsing or to tabs you have
        not acted on.
      </dd>
      <dt>Script injection</dt>
      <dd>
        The check must run inside the page: what matters is the rendered result
        — the accessibility tree, the computed styles, the contrast actually
        shown — and none of that is visible from outside.
      </dd>
      <dt>Local storage</dt>
      <dd>Your settings, as above.</dd>
      <dt>Side panel</dt>
      <dd>Where the findings are displayed, beside the page they are about.</dd>
      <dt>Site access</dt>
      <dd>
        Asked for at the moment you start a scan, for the site being scanned,
        not at install time.
      </dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>This site</h2>
    <p>
      No cookies, no analytics, no third-party scripts, no tracking pixels. The
      server keeps ordinary web-server logs — address requested, time, and the
      information your browser sends with any request — which are used to keep
      the site running and are not combined with anything else or used to
      identify anyone.
    </p>

    <h2>If you write to us</h2>
    <p>
      Mail sent to <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a> is kept as long as
      needed to answer it. Reports filed on the public issue tracker are public,
      as issue trackers are.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the General Data Protection Regulation you may ask what personal
      data we hold about you, ask for it to be corrected or erased, and complain
      to a supervisory authority. In practice we hold almost nothing: for
      extension users, nothing at all. Write to{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a> and you will get an answer.
    </p>
    <p>
      The controller is {organisation}, Swedish company registration number{" "}
      {orgNr}, Stockholm, Sweden. The supervisory authority in Sweden is{" "}
      <a
        href="https://www.imy.se/"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">Integritetsskyddsmyndigheten</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      This page is revised when what it describes changes. Last revised{" "}
      <time datetime={lastRevised}>{lastRevised}</time>. Earlier versions are in
      the repository's history.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
